{"id":"n6d58ab1a21","headline":"Indonesia Budget Deficit at 1.24% of GDP in January to September, Minister Says","summary":"Indonesia's government ran a budget deficit of 319 trillion rupiah, or US$17.83 billion, in January to September. The deficit equals 1.24% of GDP, according to the finance minister.","why":"A government's budget deficit as a share of GDP signals fiscal strength and influences borrowing needs and bond market sentiment. Indonesia is Southeast Asia's largest economy.","category":"economy","event_type":"macro-data","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Jakarta","country":"Indonesia","lat":-6.209,"lon":106.846,"region":"asia"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"PT. Kontan Grahanusa Mediatama","url":"https://english.kontan.co.id/news/indonesia-budget-deficit-at-124-of-gdp-in-january-to-september-minister-says"},"sources":[{"name":"PT. Kontan Grahanusa Mediatama","url":"https://english.kontan.co.id/news/indonesia-budget-deficit-at-124-of-gdp-in-january-to-september-minister-says"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T11:18:47Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-11T22:35:51Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"74af4342dfa9635e","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-11T22:35:51Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-10-08T11:18:47Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-10-08T12:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"ID","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/banknotes-money-256281.jpg","alt":"banknotes money (illustration)","credit":"jarmoluk","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/money-card-pocket-concept-idea-256281/"}}